<h2 class=3D"text-xl font-bold text-text-100 mt-1 -mb-0.5">K=E1=BA=BFt Lu=
=E1=BA=ADn: Mastering Front End System Design</h2>
<h3 class=3D"text-lg font-bold text-text-100 mt-1 -mb-1.5">=F0=9F=8E=AF Key=
 Takeaways t=E1=BB=AB Principal Level Experience</h3>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>1. System Design is Abou=
t Trade-offs, Not Perfect Solutions</strong></p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">T=E1=BB=AB 10+ years building pr=
oduction systems, lesson quan tr=E1=BB=8Dng nh=E1=BA=A5t: <strong>There's n=
o silver bullet</strong>. M=E1=BB=97i decision c=C3=B3 consequences, v=C3=
=A0 good architects understand those trade-offs.</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>2. User Experience Drive=
s Technical Decisions</strong></p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">Unlike backend systems (focus re=
liability v=C3=A0 scalability), front end systems ph=E1=BA=A3i prioritize u=
ser experience. Technical excellence means nothing n=E1=BA=BFu users strugg=
le with interface.</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>3. Performance is a Feat=
ure, Not an Afterthought</strong></p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">Performance budget ph=E1=BA=A3i =
be first-class citizen trong design process. Users will abandon slow applic=
ations faster than broken ones.</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>4. Accessibility is Not =
Optional</strong></p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">Building accessible interfaces i=
s legal requirement, moral obligation, v=C3=A0 business advantage. It's tam=
b=C3=A9m often the difference gi=E1=BB=AFa senior v=C3=A0 principal level t=
hinking.</p>
